%% cssn_boot.glp --- the child-safe social networking platform on two
%% smartphones (SGSG paper, Section 7): under the boot harness, one isolate per
%% person, each with its own key pair, running the social graph of graph/core as
%% its super-app and hosting CSSN's mini-app (programs/cssn/childsafe).  Each
%% person trusts the bundled compiler's key, reads the certified artefact
%% childsafe.glpw from graph/core with load_file/2 and installs it, giving the
%% super-app one end of a channel of the platform's commands and notifications;
%% alice cold-calls bob, they befriend across the isolates, alice invites him to
%% the platform, bob consents, and the handshake opens a root channel of the
%% platform's own protocol between their two executions, each activated by
%% run/3.  Adopting that conversation IS befriending under the platform's
%% contract, so each execution tells its person it is connected; alice's person
%% then sends bob one message of the platform.  The program is graph/core, named
%% as :boot's second argument:
%%   :artefact programs/cssn/childsafe programs/social/graph/core
%%   :boot programs/social/cssn_boot.glp programs/social/graph/core
%% Expected on the persons' screens: [alice] connected(bob),
%% [bob] connected(alice), [bob] received(alice, hello).

procedure boot.
boot :-
    sg_init(alice, cssn, _)@alice,
    sg_init(bob, cssn, _)@bob.
